IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ga-dates`

-- Guardianship Act 1987 (NSW) -- Parts 3 (guardianship orders), 3A (financial management), 4 and 4A (directions, and
-- the immunity they give), 5A (orders made elsewhere), 7 (review of the Public Guardian's decisions) and 9 (personal
-- immunity, confidentiality), from the seat of the person the orders are about.
--
-- SEAT: the person about whom a guardianship order or a financial management order is sought or made (the "person under
-- guardianship", the "protected person"), and a person removed from premises under ss 11-13. Every exported question is
-- one that person would ask: "Who can apply about me?", "Can an order be made about me, and of what kind?", "Can this
-- person be my guardian?", "How long can it last, and is it still in force?", "Must it be reviewed if I ask?", "Can I sue
-- for what was done under it?", "How long can I be kept after being removed?", "Can my estate be managed, and when do I
-- get it back?", "Can I challenge the Public Guardian's decision?", "Can information about me be disclosed?". The
-- Tribunal, the Public Guardian, the NSW Trustee and the Secretary get no seat.
--
-- ANSWERS. JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no; NOTHING, with a NOTHING-kind comment, where it does
-- not answer. The Tribunal's judgments are asked as facts.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; version as at 27 March 2021; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Guardianship Act 1987 -- orders about me`

§§ `The nouns`

DECLARE `Who is applying` IS ONE OF
    `I am`
    `the Public Guardian`
    `the NSW Trustee`
    `the manager of my estate`
    `my guardian`
    `someone the Tribunal considers has a genuine concern for my welfare`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `The duration` IS ONE OF
    `a continuing order`
    `a temporary order`

DECLARE `The extent` IS ONE OF
    `a plenary order`
    `a limited order`

DECLARE `Which order` IS ONE OF
    `the initial order`
    `a renewed order`

-- What the Tribunal must, may or need not do with a review.
DECLARE `The Tribunal's duty to review` IS ONE OF
    `the Tribunal must review it`
    `the Tribunal may refuse to review it`
    `the Tribunal is not required to review it when it expires`

-- The parties and acts of the two regulative rules.
DECLARE `Orders party` IS ONE OF `the Secretary`, `the Tribunal`
DECLARE `Orders act` IS ONE OF
    `apply for a guardianship order about me`
    `complete its further consideration of my capability`

§§ `s 9 -- who can apply for a guardianship order about me`

-- s 9(1) "An application for a guardianship order in respect of a person may be made to the Tribunal-- (a) by the person,
-- ... (c) by the Public Guardian, or (d) by any other person who, in the opinion of the Tribunal, has a genuine concern
-- for the welfare of the person." s 9(2) "An application may not be made in respect of a person who is under the age of
-- 16 years." The list is not closed with "only": a person outside it is NOTHING. s 9(2) is a flat negative.
@export Can this person apply to the Tribunal for a guardianship order about me (s 9)?
GIVEN `who is applying` IS A `Who is applying` @desc Who would apply. One of: "I am", "the Public Guardian", "the NSW Trustee", "the manager of my estate", "my guardian", "someone the Tribunal considers has a genuine concern for my welfare", "someone else"
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day of the application` IS A DATE @desc The day the application would be made
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can this person apply for a guardianship order about me` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`born on` `my date of birth` `is at least` 16 `years old on` `the day of the application`))
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 9(2) "may not be made"
    ELSE CONSIDER `who is applying`
         WHEN `I am` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `the Public Guardian` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `someone the Tribunal considers has a genuine concern for my welfare` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 9(1) lists without "only"; anyone else may still be found to have a genuine concern)

§§ `ss 14, 15(1) -- can a guardianship order be made about me`

-- s 14(1) "If, after conducting a hearing into any application made to it for a guardianship order in respect of a
-- person, the Tribunal is satisfied that the person is a person in need of a guardian, it may make a guardianship order".
-- s 15(1) "A guardianship order shall not be made in respect of a person-- (a) if the person is under the age of 16
-- years, or (b) [subject of a Supreme Court guardianship order] unless the Supreme Court consents ..., or (c) [subject of
-- a Children's Court order under s 79A of the Children and Young Persons (Care and Protection) Act 1998] unless the
-- Children's Court consents". s 14(2): the matters the Tribunal must have regard to (my views, my spouse's, my carer's,
-- family relationships, culture and language, and whether services could be given without an order) are its judgment, in
-- comments only.
@export Can the Tribunal make a guardianship order about me (ss 14(1), 15(1))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day of the order` IS A DATE @desc The day the order would be made
      `the Tribunal has held a hearing into the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has conducted a hearing into the application
      `the Tribunal is satisfied I am a person in need of a guardian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is satisfied that, because of a disability, you are totally or partially incapable of managing your person
      `a Supreme Court guardianship order is in force about me without its consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the subject of a Supreme Court order about guardianship of your person, and the Supreme Court has not consented to the Tribunal's order
      `a Children's Court section 79A order is in force about me without its consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the subject of a Children's Court order under s 79A of the Children and Young Persons (Care and Protection) Act 1998, and the Children's Court has not consented
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Tribunal make a guardianship order about me` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`born on` `my date of birth` `is at least` 16 `years old on` `the day of the order`)) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 15(1)(a)
           IF `a Supreme Court guardianship order is in force about me without its consent` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 15(1)(b)
           IF `a Children's Court section 79A order is in force about me without its consent` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 15(1)(c)
           IF `the Tribunal has held a hearing into the application` AND `the Tribunal is satisfied I am a person in need of a guardian` THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 14(1) "may"
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- s 14(1) "If, after conducting a hearing ..., the Tribunal is satisfied"

§§ `ss 15(2)-(4), 17(4) -- what kind of order`

-- s 15(2) "A temporary guardianship order shall not be made in circumstances in which it is practicable to make a
-- continuing guardianship order appointing a person other than the Public Guardian". s 15(3) "A continuing guardianship
-- order appointing the Public Guardian ... shall not be made in circumstances in which such an order can be made appointing
-- some other person". s 15(4) "A plenary guardianship order shall not be made in circumstances in which a limited
-- guardianship order would suffice." s 17(4) "The Public Guardian shall be appointed as the guardian of a person the
-- subject of a temporary guardianship order." Each is a flat negative; where none applies the Act sets no other bar
-- (fork F7). ss 15(2) and 15(3) are read as turning on the same fact (fork F7).
@export Can the Tribunal make this kind of guardianship order about me (ss 15(2)-(4), 17(4))?
GIVEN `the duration` IS A `The duration` @desc Whether the order is continuing or temporary. One of: "a continuing order", "a temporary order"
      `the extent` IS A `The extent` @desc Whether the order is plenary (all a guardian's functions) or limited (only those the order lists). One of: "a plenary order", "a limited order"
      `the guardian would be the Public Guardian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order would appoint the Public Guardian as your guardian
      `a continuing order appointing someone other than the Public Guardian could be made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a continuing order appointing someone other than the Public Guardian (for example a family member) could practicably be made
      `a limited order would suffice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a limited order would be enough
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Tribunal make this kind of guardianship order` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `temporary` AND `a continuing order appointing someone other than the Public Guardian could be made` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 15(2)
           IF `temporary` AND (NOT `the guardian would be the Public Guardian`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 17(4)
           IF (NOT `temporary`) AND `the guardian would be the Public Guardian` AND `a continuing order appointing someone other than the Public Guardian could be made` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 15(3)
           IF `plenary` AND `a limited order would suffice` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 15(4)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE  -- no bar in ss 15, 17 applies (fork F7)
    WHERE
        `temporary` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the duration`
            WHEN `a temporary order` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `plenary` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the extent`
            WHEN `a plenary order` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 16(1)(a), 17(1), (2) -- who can be my guardian`

-- s 16(1)(a): a guardianship order "shall appoint a person who is of or above the age of 18 years". s 17(1) "A person
-- shall not be appointed as the guardian ... unless the Tribunal is satisfied that-- (a) the personality of the proposed
-- guardian is generally compatible with that of the person under guardianship, (b) there is no undue conflict between the
-- interests (particularly, the financial interests) of the proposed guardian and those of the person under guardianship,
-- and (c) the proposed guardian is both willing and able to exercise the functions". s 17(2): (1) does not apply to the
-- Public Guardian.
@export Can the Tribunal appoint this person as my guardian (ss 16(1)(a), 17(1), (2))?
GIVEN `they are the Public Guardian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the proposed guardian is the Public Guardian
      `their date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The proposed guardian's date of birth (any date if the Public Guardian)
      `the day of the order` IS A DATE @desc The day the order would be made
      `the Tribunal is satisfied their personality is generally compatible with mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is satisfied that the proposed guardian's personality is generally compatible with yours
      `the Tribunal is satisfied there is no undue conflict of interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is satisfied that there is no undue conflict between their interests (particularly financial interests) and yours
      `the Tribunal is satisfied they are willing and able` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is satisfied that they are both willing and able to act as your guardian
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can this person be appointed as my guardian` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `they are the Public Guardian` THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 17(2)
           IF (NOT (`born on` `their date of birth` `is at least` 18 `years old on` `the day of the order`)) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 16(1)(a) "shall appoint a person who is of or above the age of 18 years"
           IF     `the Tribunal is satisfied their personality is generally compatible with mine`
              AND `the Tribunal is satisfied there is no undue conflict of interest`
              AND `the Tribunal is satisfied they are willing and able` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- s 17(1) "shall not be appointed ... unless"

§§ `s 18 -- how long my guardianship order can last`

-- s 18(1) "A continuing guardianship order has effect-- (a) in the case of an initial order--for such period (not
-- exceeding 1 year from the date when it was made) as the Tribunal may specify ..., or (b) in the case of an order that is
-- renewed--for such period (not exceeding 3 years from the date when it was renewed)". s 18(1A), (1B): up to 3 years
-- (initial) or 5 years (renewed) "from the date on which it was made" if the Tribunal is satisfied that the person has
-- permanent disabilities, is unlikely to become capable of managing their person, and needs a longer order. s 18(2): a
-- temporary order, initial or renewed, not exceeding 30 days. A renewed order's longer period is counted from the
-- renewal (fork F8; finding 3).
@export What is the last day my guardianship order can have effect, at most (s 18)?
GIVEN `the duration` IS A `The duration` @desc Whether the order is continuing or temporary. One of: "a continuing order", "a temporary order"
      `which order` IS A `Which order` @desc Whether this is the initial order or a renewed one. One of: "the initial order", "a renewed order"
      `the day it was made or renewed` IS A DATE @desc The day the order was made (or, for a renewed order, renewed)
      `the Tribunal is satisfied of the section 18(1B) matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a continuing order: whether the Tribunal is satisfied that you have permanent disabilities, that you are unlikely to become capable of managing your person, and that an order longer than 1 year (initial) or 3 years (renewed) is needed
GIVETH A DATE
`The last day my guardianship order can have effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the duration`
    WHEN `a temporary order` THEN `the day it was made or renewed` `plus days` 30
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `which order`
        WHEN `the initial order` THEN
            IF `the Tribunal is satisfied of the section 18(1B) matters`
            THEN `the day it was made or renewed` `plus years` 3
            ELSE `the day it was made or renewed` `plus years` 1
        OTHERWISE
            IF `the Tribunal is satisfied of the section 18(1B) matters`
            THEN `the day it was made or renewed` `plus years` 5
            ELSE `the day it was made or renewed` `plus years` 3

-- s 18(3) "A temporary guardianship order may be renewed only once."
@export Can my temporary guardianship order be renewed (s 18(3))?
GIVEN `times it has already been renewed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times the temporary order has already been renewed
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my temporary guardianship order be renewed` MEANS
    IF `times it has already been renewed` AT LEAST 1
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- "only once"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `ss 23, 25(6), 25C -- is my guardianship order still in force`

-- s 25(6) "If a review of a guardianship order is commenced but not completed before the expiration of the period
-- specified in the order as the period for which the order has effect, the order is taken to be extended until the
-- completion of the review." s 25(4): a review "is taken to have commenced on the issue of" the notice of it. s 23(b): an
-- order "does not have effect ... while the person is ... the subject of a subsequent order made by the Supreme Court ...
-- appointing a guardian". s 25C: the Tribunal may suspend or revoke, or determine that the order lapses. The order is
-- read as in force on the day the review is completed (fork F9).
@export Is my guardianship order in force on this day (ss 18, 23, 25(4), (6), 25C)?
GIVEN `the last day of the period in the order` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period the order says it has effect for
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
      `a review began on or before that last day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal issued a notice of a review of the order on or before the last day of its period
      `the review has been completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that review has been completed
      `the day the review was completed` IS A DATE @desc The day the review was completed (any date if it has not been)
      `the order has been revoked, suspended or allowed to lapse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has revoked or suspended the order, or determined that it lapse, with effect before the day you are asking about
      `a later Supreme Court order appoints a guardian of my person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are now the subject of a later Supreme Court order appointing a guardian of your person
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my guardianship order in force on this day` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `a later Supreme Court order appoints a guardian of my person` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 23 "does not have effect"
           IF `the order has been revoked, suspended or allowed to lapse` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 25C
           IF `the day I am asking about` `is on or before` `the last day of the period in the order` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `a review began on or before that last day` AND (NOT `the review has been completed`) THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 25(6) "extended until the completion of the review"
           IF `a review began on or before that last day` AND (`the day I am asking about` `is on or before` `the day the review was completed`) THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 25(6) (fork F9)
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- the period the order and s 18 fix has ended

§§ `ss 16(2A), 25, 25A, 25B -- must my guardianship order be reviewed`

-- s 25(2) "The Tribunal must review each guardianship order-- (a) at the request of any person entitled to request a
-- review of the order, and (b) at the expiration of the period for which the order has effect." s 25(3)(b): not required
-- under (2)(b) if the order contains a s 16(2A) statement. s 25A: the Tribunal may refuse a request "if-- (a) in the
-- opinion of the Tribunal, the request does not disclose grounds that warrant a review, or (b) the Tribunal has previously
-- reviewed the order." s 25B: entitled to request: the guardian, the person under guardianship, the Public Guardian, any
-- other person who, in the Tribunal's opinion, has a genuine concern for the welfare of the person. Someone else is
-- outside s 25B, which is not closed with "only": NOTHING.
DECLARE `Why a review` IS ONE OF
    `someone has asked for a review`
    `the order's period is ending`

@export Must the Tribunal review my guardianship order (ss 16(2A), 25(2), (3), 25A, 25B)?
GIVEN `why a review` IS A `Why a review` @desc Why the review would happen. One of: "someone has asked for a review", "the order's period is ending"
      `who is asking` IS A `Who is applying` @desc If someone asked: who asked. One of: "I am", "my guardian", "the Public Guardian", "someone the Tribunal considers has a genuine concern for my welfare", "the NSW Trustee", "the manager of my estate", "someone else"
      `the Tribunal considers the request discloses no grounds for a review` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is of the opinion that the request does not disclose grounds that warrant a review
      `the Tribunal has reviewed the order before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has previously reviewed the order
      `the order says it will not be reviewed when it expires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order contains a statement (under s 16(2A)) that it will not be reviewed at the end of its period
GIVETH A MAYBE `The Tribunal's duty to review`
`Must the Tribunal review my guardianship order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `why a review`
    WHEN `the order's period is ending` THEN
        IF `the order says it will not be reviewed when it expires`
        THEN JUST `the Tribunal is not required to review it when it expires`  -- s 25(3)(b)
        ELSE JUST `the Tribunal must review it`  -- s 25(2)(b)
    OTHERWISE
        IF `entitled`
        THEN IF `the Tribunal considers the request discloses no grounds for a review` OR `the Tribunal has reviewed the order before`
             THEN JUST `the Tribunal may refuse to review it`  -- s 25A
             ELSE JUST `the Tribunal must review it`  -- s 25(2)(a)
        ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 25B lists without "only"; the Tribunal "may" still review on its own motion, s 25(1))
    WHERE
        `entitled` MEANS
            CONSIDER `who is asking`
            WHEN `I am` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `my guardian` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the Public Guardian` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `someone the Tribunal considers has a genuine concern for my welfare` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 21A(2), 30, 31F, 100 -- can I sue for what was done to me`

-- s 21A(2) "If a person referred to in subsection (1) (a), (b) or (c) takes any measure or action specified in the order
-- in the reasonable belief that-- (a) he or she is empowered by the guardianship order to take the measure or action, and
-- (b) the measure or action is in the best interest of the person under guardianship, and (c) it is necessary or
-- desirable to take that measure or action in the circumstances, the person concerned is not liable to any action,
-- liability, claim or demand arising out of the taking of that measure or action." A flat "is not liable": JUST FALSE.
-- Outside it the general law decides: NOTHING.
@export Can I sue the person who took a measure to make me comply with my guardian's decision (s 21A)?
GIVEN `my guardianship order specifies the measure and empowers that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your guardianship order specifies the measure or action taken and empowers that person (your guardian, a person named or of a named class, or a person your guardian authorised) to take it
      `they reasonably believed the order empowered them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they took it in the reasonable belief that the order empowered them to
      `they reasonably believed it was in my best interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they took it in the reasonable belief that it was in your best interest
      `they reasonably believed it was necessary or desirable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they took it in the reasonable belief that it was necessary or desirable in the circumstances
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I sue for a measure taken to enforce my guardianship order` MEANS
    IF     `my guardianship order specifies the measure and empowers that person`
       AND `they reasonably believed the order empowered them`
       AND `they reasonably believed it was in my best interest`
       AND `they reasonably believed it was necessary or desirable`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 21A(2) "is not liable to any action, liability, claim or demand"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (outside s 21A(2) the general law decides whether there is a claim)

-- s 30 "No proceedings shall lie against the guardian of a person under guardianship for or on account of any act, matter
-- or thing done or omitted to be done by the guardian in good faith and in accordance with a direction given under this
-- Part." s 31F "No proceedings lie against any person for or on account of any act, matter or thing done or omitted to be
-- done by the person in good faith and in accordance with the direction given under this Part" (adoption information
-- directions).
DECLARE `The direction` IS ONE OF
    `a direction to my guardian under Part 4`
    `an adoption information direction under Part 4A`

@export Can I sue for something done (or not done) in good faith under a Tribunal direction (ss 30, 31F)?
GIVEN `the direction` IS A `The direction` @desc Which kind of Tribunal direction. One of: "a direction to my guardian under Part 4", "an adoption information direction under Part 4A"
      `the person I would sue is my guardian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person you would sue is your guardian under a guardianship order
      `it was done in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act (or omission) was done in good faith
      `it was in accordance with the direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was done in accordance with the Tribunal's direction
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I sue for something done under a Tribunal direction` MEANS
    IF     `it was done in good faith`
       AND `it was in accordance with the direction`
       AND `the person is protected`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 30 "No proceedings shall lie"; s 31F "No proceedings lie"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (outside ss 30 and 31F the general law decides)
    WHERE
        `the person is protected` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the direction`
            WHEN `a direction to my guardian under Part 4` THEN `the person I would sue is my guardian`
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 100 "No matter or thing done by the Minister, the Secretary, the Public Guardian, an employee or any other person
-- shall, if the matter or thing was done in good faith and with reasonable care for the purposes of executing this Act,
-- subject the Minister, the Secretary, the Public Guardian, the employee or that other person personally to any action,
-- liability, claim or demand." Personal liability only: whether the State or another body is liable is not said (finding
-- 6).
@export Can I hold the person personally liable for something they did in carrying out the Guardianship Act (s 100)?
GIVEN `it was done in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the thing was done in good faith
      `it was done with reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was done with reasonable care
      `it was done for the purposes of executing the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was done for the purposes of carrying out the Guardianship Act (for example by the Public Guardian, a Tribunal employee, or a guardian)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I hold them personally liable` MEANS
    IF `it was done in good faith` AND `it was done with reasonable care` AND `it was done for the purposes of executing the Act`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 100 "shall ... [not] subject ... personally to any action, liability, claim or demand"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (outside s 100 the general law decides)

§§ `s 13(2) -- how long I can be kept after being removed`

-- s 13(1): a person removed from premises under s 11 or s 12 is placed "forthwith" in the care of the Secretary. s 13(2)
-- "If a person has been removed from any premises under section 12 and placed in the care of the Secretary, the Secretary
-- shall not keep the person in his or her care for more than 3 days unless the Secretary has, before the expiration of
-- that period, made an application for a guardianship order in respect of the person." Written as a rule: the Secretary
-- must apply within 3 days of the placement, or the keeping must end. Time 0 is the day of placement, in days; the 3 days
-- run to the end of the third day after it (fork F10). s 13(2) speaks only of a removal under s 12 (a search warrant), not
-- of one under s 11 (a Tribunal order).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Orders party` `Orders act`
`s 13(2) -- the Secretary must apply for a guardianship order within 3 days, or not keep the person` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `apply for a guardianship order about me`
    WITHIN 3
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary kept a person removed under s 12 for more than 3 days without having applied for a guardianship order before the 3 days expired (s 13(2))"

DECLARE `How I was removed` IS ONE OF
    `under a search warrant (section 12)`
    `under a Tribunal removal order (section 11)`

DECLARE `What section 13(2) means for me` IS ONE OF
    `the three days have not yet passed, so section 13(2) does not yet stop the Secretary keeping me`
    `the Secretary applied for a guardianship order in time, so section 13(2) does not stop the Secretary keeping me`
    `the three days have passed without an application, so the Secretary must not keep me`
    `section 13(2) sets no limit, because I was removed under a Tribunal order`

@export I was removed from premises and placed in the Secretary's care: may the Secretary still keep me on this day (s 13(2))?
GIVEN `how I was removed` IS A `How I was removed` @desc How you were removed. One of: "under a search warrant (section 12)", "under a Tribunal removal order (section 11)"
      `the day I was placed in the Secretary's care` IS A DATE @desc The day you were placed in the care of the Secretary
      `the Secretary has applied for a guardianship order about me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary has applied to the Tribunal for a guardianship order about you
      `the day the Secretary applied` IS A DATE @desc The day the Secretary applied (any date if it has not)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
GIVETH A `What section 13(2) means for me`
`May the Secretary still keep me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how I was removed`
    WHEN `under a Tribunal removal order (section 11)` THEN `section 13(2) sets no limit, because I was removed under a Tribunal order`
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 13(2) -- the Secretary must apply for a guardianship order within 3 days, or not keep the person` 0 `the events`
        WHEN FULFILLED THEN `the Secretary applied for a guardianship order in time, so section 13(2) does not stop the Secretary keeping me`
        OTHERWISE
            IF `the day asked` GREATER THAN 3
            THEN `the three days have passed without an application, so the Secretary must not keep me`  -- the LEST: the deadline has passed
            ELSE `the three days have not yet passed, so section 13(2) does not yet stop the Secretary keeping me`  -- the rule is still waiting
    WHERE
        `the day asked` MEANS `the days from` `the day I was placed in the Secretary's care` `to` `the day I am asking about`
        `the day applied` MEANS `the days from` `the day I was placed in the Secretary's care` `to` `the day the Secretary applied`
        `the events` MEANS
            IF `the Secretary has applied for a guardianship order about me` AND `the day applied` AT MOST `the day asked`
            THEN LIST (EVENT `the Secretary` `apply for a guardianship order about me` `the day applied`), (WAITUNTIL `the day asked`)
            ELSE LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day asked`)

§§ `ss 25F, 25G, 25I, 25K -- can a financial management order be made about me`

-- s 25F "The Tribunal may make a financial management order ...-- (a) in connection with its making a guardianship order
-- ..., or (b) following (or in the course of) proceedings under Part 3 ..., or (c) if an application for such an order has
-- been made to it under section 25I ..., or (d) following (or in the course of) proceedings under section 36 of the Powers
-- of Attorney Act 2003". s 25G "The Tribunal may make a financial management order in respect of a person only if the
-- Tribunal has considered the person's capability to manage his or her own affairs and is satisfied that-- (a) the person
-- is not capable of managing those affairs, and (b) there is a need for another person to manage those affairs on the
-- person's behalf, and (c) it is in the person's best interests that the order be made." s 25K(1): no jurisdiction (other
-- than for an interim order) while the question of the person's capability is before the Supreme Court; s 25K(2): no
-- jurisdiction at all while an order under the NSW Trustee and Guardian Act 2009 or the Mental Health Act 2007 is in force
-- over any part of the estate. s 25E(2): a part of the estate may be excluded.
DECLARE `The occasion` IS ONE OF
    `guardianship proceedings about me (with or without an order)`
    `an application for a financial management order under section 25I`
    `proceedings under section 36 of the Powers of Attorney Act 2003`
    `no such proceedings`

@export Can the Tribunal make a financial management order over my estate (ss 25F, 25G, 25K)?
GIVEN `the occasion` IS A `The occasion` @desc The proceedings in which the order would be made. One of: "guardianship proceedings about me (with or without an order)", "an application for a financial management order under section 25I", "proceedings under section 36 of the Powers of Attorney Act 2003", "no such proceedings"
      `the Tribunal has considered my capability to manage my affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has considered your capability to manage your own affairs (money and property)
      `the Tribunal is satisfied I am not capable of managing my affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is satisfied that you are not capable of managing your own affairs
      `the Tribunal is satisfied someone else needs to manage them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is satisfied that there is a need for another person to manage your affairs on your behalf
      `the Tribunal is satisfied the order is in my best interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is satisfied that the order is in your best interests
      `my capability is before the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the question of your capability to manage your own affairs is before the Supreme Court
      `a NSW Trustee and Guardian Act or Mental Health Act order covers part of my estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an order under the NSW Trustee and Guardian Act 2009 or the Mental Health Act 2007 is in force over any part of your estate
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Tribunal make a financial management order about me` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `a NSW Trustee and Guardian Act or Mental Health Act order covers part of my estate` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 25K(2) "does not have jurisdiction"
           IF `my capability is before the Supreme Court` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 25K(1) (an interim order aside)
           IF `no occasion` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 25F lists the occasions without "only"; fork F11)
           IF     `the Tribunal has considered my capability to manage my affairs`
              AND `the Tribunal is satisfied I am not capable of managing my affairs`
              AND `the Tribunal is satisfied someone else needs to manage them`
              AND `the Tribunal is satisfied the order is in my best interests` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- s 25G "only if"
    WHERE
        `no occasion` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the occasion`
            WHEN `no such proceedings` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 25I(1) "An application for a financial management order may be made by-- (a) the NSW Trustee, or (a1) the person who
-- is the subject of the application, or (b) any person who, in the opinion of the Tribunal, has a genuine concern for the
-- welfare of the person". Not closed with "only": NOTHING for anyone else.
@export Can this person apply for a financial management order about me (s 25I(1))?
GIVEN `who is applying` IS A `Who is applying` @desc Who would apply. One of: "I am", "the NSW Trustee", "someone the Tribunal considers has a genuine concern for my welfare", "the Public Guardian", "my guardian", "the manager of my estate", "someone else"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can this person apply for a financial management order about me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who is applying`
    WHEN `I am` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the NSW Trustee` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `someone the Tribunal considers has a genuine concern for my welfare` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 25I(1) lists without "only")

§§ `s 25H -- interim financial management orders`

-- s 25H(1): the Tribunal may make "a financial management order for a specified period not exceeding 6 months (an interim
-- financial management order), pending the Tribunal's further consideration of the capability of the person". s 25H(2)
-- "An interim financial management order may be made only in respect of a person-- (a) who is under guardianship, or (b)
-- who is the subject of an application under Part 3 or this Part." s 25K(2) bars every financial management order while
-- a NSW Trustee and Guardian Act or Mental Health Act order covers part of the estate.
@export Can the Tribunal make an interim financial management order about me for this period (ss 25H(1), (2), 25K(2))?
GIVEN `I am under guardianship or the subject of an application under Part 3 or Part 3A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are under guardianship, or the subject of an application for a guardianship order or a financial management order
      `the day the order would be made` IS A DATE @desc The day the interim order would be made
      `the last day of the period it would specify` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period the interim order would specify
      `a NSW Trustee and Guardian Act or Mental Health Act order covers part of my estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an order under the NSW Trustee and Guardian Act 2009 or the Mental Health Act 2007 is in force over any part of your estate
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Tribunal make an interim financial management order about me` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `a NSW Trustee and Guardian Act or Mental Health Act order covers part of my estate` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 25K(2)
           IF (NOT `I am under guardianship or the subject of an application under Part 3 or Part 3A`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 25H(2) "only"
           IF `the last day of the period it would specify` `is on or before` (`the day the order would be made` `plus months` 6) THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- s 25H(1) "not exceeding 6 months" (fork F1)

-- s 25H(3) "If the further consideration of the capability of the person ... is not completed before the expiry of the
-- period specified in the order, the order is taken to be revoked on that expiry." Written as a rule: the Tribunal must
-- complete its further consideration within the specified period; if it does not, the order is revoked (the LEST). Time
-- 0 is the day the order was made, in days; "before the expiry" is read as on or before the last day of the period.
-- s 25N(5) (an order "taken to be extended until the completion" of a review) may pull the other way (finding 4).
GIVEN `the days in the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Orders party` `Orders act`
`s 25H(3) -- the Tribunal must complete its further consideration within the period, or the interim order is revoked` `the days in the period` MEANS
    PARTY `the Tribunal`
    MUST `complete its further consideration of my capability`
    WITHIN `the days in the period`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Tribunal` BECAUSE "the further consideration was not completed before the period expired, so the interim financial management order is taken to be revoked on that expiry (s 25H(3))"

DECLARE `Where my interim order stands` IS ONE OF
    `it is in force, pending the Tribunal's further consideration`
    `the Tribunal completed its further consideration in time, and what follows is its decision`
    `it was taken to be revoked when its period expired`

@export Is my interim financial management order still in force on this day (s 25H(3))?
GIVEN `the day the interim order was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the interim financial management order was made
      `the last day of its period` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period the interim order specifies
      `the Tribunal has completed its further consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has completed its further consideration of your capability to manage your affairs
      `the day it completed it` IS A DATE @desc The day the Tribunal completed that further consideration (any date if it has not)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
GIVETH A `Where my interim order stands`
`Is my interim financial management order still in force` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 25H(3) -- the Tribunal must complete its further consideration within the period, or the interim order is revoked` `the days in the period`) 0 `the events`
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN `the Tribunal completed its further consideration in time, and what follows is its decision`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the day asked` GREATER THAN `the days in the period`
        THEN `it was taken to be revoked when its period expired`  -- the LEST: the deadline has passed
        ELSE `it is in force, pending the Tribunal's further consideration`  -- the rule is still waiting
    WHERE
        `the days in the period` MEANS `the days from` `the day the interim order was made` `to` `the last day of its period`
        `the day asked` MEANS `the days from` `the day the interim order was made` `to` `the day I am asking about`
        `the day completed` MEANS `the days from` `the day the interim order was made` `to` `the day it completed it`
        `the events` MEANS
            IF `the Tribunal has completed its further consideration` AND `the day completed` AT MOST `the day asked`
            THEN LIST (EVENT `the Tribunal` `complete its further consideration of my capability` `the day completed`), (WAITUNTIL `the day asked`)
            ELSE LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day asked`)

§§ `ss 25N, 25O, 25P, 25R -- reviewing and revoking my financial management order`

-- s 25R: entitled to apply to revoke or vary: (a) the protected person, (b) the NSW Trustee, (c) the manager, (d) any
-- other person who, in the Tribunal's opinion, has a genuine concern for the welfare of the protected person. s 25N(4)(b):
-- the Tribunal "must, on an application under section 25R ... review". s 25O: it may refuse if the application does not
-- disclose grounds that warrant a review, or it has previously reviewed the order.
@export If this person applies to revoke or vary my financial management order, must the Tribunal review it (ss 25N(4), 25O, 25R)?
GIVEN `who is applying` IS A `Who is applying` @desc Who would apply. One of: "I am", "the NSW Trustee", "the manager of my estate", "someone the Tribunal considers has a genuine concern for my welfare", "the Public Guardian", "my guardian", "someone else"
      `the Tribunal considers the application discloses no grounds for a review` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is of the opinion that the application does not disclose grounds that warrant a review
      `the Tribunal has reviewed the order before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has previously reviewed the order
GIVETH A MAYBE `The Tribunal's duty to review`
`Must the Tribunal review my financial management order` MEANS
    IF `entitled`
    THEN IF `the Tribunal considers the application discloses no grounds for a review` OR `the Tribunal has reviewed the order before`
         THEN JUST `the Tribunal may refuse to review it`  -- s 25O
         ELSE JUST `the Tribunal must review it`  -- s 25N(4)(b)
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 25R lists without "only"; the Tribunal may review on its own motion, s 25N(4)(a))
    WHERE
        `entitled` MEANS
            CONSIDER `who is applying`
            WHEN `I am` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the NSW Trustee` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the manager of my estate` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `someone the Tribunal considers has a genuine concern for my welfare` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 25P(2) "The Tribunal may revoke a financial management order only if-- (a) the Tribunal is satisfied that the
-- protected person is capable of managing his or her affairs, or (b) the Tribunal considers that it is in the best
-- interests of the protected person that the order be revoked (even though the Tribunal is not satisfied that the
-- protected person is capable of managing his or her affairs)."
@export Can the Tribunal revoke my financial management order (s 25P(2))?
GIVEN `the Tribunal is satisfied I am capable of managing my affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is satisfied that you are capable of managing your affairs
      `the Tribunal considers revoking it is in my best interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal considers that revoking the order is in your best interests
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Tribunal revoke my financial management order` MEANS
    IF `the Tribunal is satisfied I am capable of managing my affairs` OR `the Tribunal considers revoking it is in my best interests`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- "only if"

§§ `ss 25M(2), (3), 25Q -- the manager of my estate, and getting it back`

-- s 25M(2) "an order under subsection (1) (a) [appointing a suitable person as manager] does not authorise the person
-- appointed as manager to interfere in any way with the estate concerned unless-- (a) such directions of the Supreme Court
-- as are relevant to the management of the estate have been obtained, or (b) the NSW Trustee has ... authorised the person
-- to exercise functions in respect of the estate." s 25M(3) "However, the person appointed as manager may take such action
-- as may be necessary for the protection of the estate (including action specified by the Tribunal) pending the
-- directions of the Court or authorisation by the NSW Trustee." Where the estate is committed to the NSW Trustee itself,
-- s 25M(2) does not speak (the NSW Trustee and Guardian Act 2009 does): NOTHING.
@export Can the manager the Tribunal appointed for my estate take this action with it (s 25M(2), (3))?
GIVEN `my estate was committed to the NSW Trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal committed the management of your estate to the NSW Trustee (rather than appointing another person as manager)
      `the Supreme Court has given relevant directions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the manager has obtained the Supreme Court's directions relevant to managing your estate
      `the NSW Trustee has authorised the manager` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the NSW Trustee has authorised the manager to exercise functions over your estate
      `the action is necessary to protect my estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action is necessary to protect your estate (including action the Tribunal specified) while directions or authorisation are awaited
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my estate manager take this action` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `my estate was committed to the NSW Trustee` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 25M(2) speaks only of a manager appointed under s 25M(1)(a); points outside the sources)
           IF `the Supreme Court has given relevant directions` OR `the NSW Trustee has authorised the manager` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `the action is necessary to protect my estate` THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 25M(3)
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- s 25M(2) "does not authorise ... unless"

-- s 25Q(1) "If a financial management order is revoked (or varied so as to exclude ... a specified part of the estate
-- ...), the person appointed as manager of the estate is to pay over or hand over the estate (or the relevant part ...)--
-- (a) to the owner of the estate, or (b) to a person (designated by the Tribunal) on behalf of the owner". s 25Q(4): the
-- handing over does not change ownership. s 25Q(3): the manager incurs no liability for it.
DECLARE `Who gets my estate back` IS ONE OF
    `the manager must hand it over to me`
    `the manager must hand it over to the person the Tribunal designated, on my behalf`

@export My financial management order has been revoked (or part of my estate excluded): to whom must the manager hand my estate over (s 25Q)?
GIVEN `the Tribunal designated someone to receive it on my behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal designated a person to receive the estate on your behalf
GIVETH A `Who gets my estate back`
`To whom must my estate be handed over` MEANS
    IF `the Tribunal designated someone to receive it on my behalf`
    THEN `the manager must hand it over to the person the Tribunal designated, on my behalf`
    ELSE `the manager must hand it over to me`

§§ `s 48B -- a guardian or manager appointed elsewhere`

-- s 48B(1), (2): a person appointed under a corresponding law (declared by the regulations; not deposited) as guardian or
-- manager "may apply to the Tribunal for recognition", and "The Tribunal must recognise the applicant if satisfied that
-- the applicant has been so appointed." s 48B(4): the recognised guardian or manager exercises only functions authorised
-- both by the appointment and by this Act. A failed "if" is JUST FALSE; a law not declared corresponding is outside
-- s 48B: NOTHING.
@export My guardian or estate manager was appointed under another State's, Territory's or country's law: must the Tribunal recognise them in NSW (s 48B)?
GIVEN `that law is declared a corresponding law by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law they were appointed under is declared by the NSW Guardianship Regulation to be a corresponding law
      `the Tribunal is satisfied they were so appointed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is satisfied that they were appointed under that law as your guardian or the manager of your estate
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must the Tribunal recognise my guardian or manager from elsewhere` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `that law is declared a corresponding law by the regulations`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (outside s 48B; the regulation is not deposited)
           IF `the Tribunal is satisfied they were so appointed` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- s 48B(2) "if satisfied"

§§ `s 80A -- challenging the Public Guardian's decision`

-- s 80A(1) "An application may be made to the Civil and Administrative Tribunal for an administrative review under the
-- Administrative Decisions Review Act 1997 of a decision of the Public Guardian that-- (a) is made in connection with the
-- exercise of the Public Guardian's functions under this Act as a guardian, and (b) is of a class of decision prescribed
-- by the regulations". s 80A(2) "An application under this section may be made by-- (a) the person to whom the decision
-- relates, or (b) the spouse of the person, or (c) the person who has the care of the person ..., or (d) any other person
-- whose interests are, in the opinion of the Civil and Administrative Tribunal, adversely affected by the decision." The
-- time limit for the application is in the Administrative Decisions Review Act 1997, not here. A decision outside (1),
-- or an applicant outside (2), is outside a grant with no "only": NOTHING.
DECLARE `Who is seeking review` IS ONE OF
    `I am, as the person the decision is about`
    `my spouse`
    `the person who has the care of me`
    `someone the Tribunal considers adversely affected by the decision`
    `someone not listed in section 80A`

@export Can this person apply to NCAT for administrative review of the Public Guardian's decision about me (s 80A)?
GIVEN `the decision was made by the Public Guardian as my guardian under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Public Guardian made the decision in exercising its functions under the Guardianship Act as your guardian
      `the decision is of a class prescribed by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision is of a class prescribed by the Guardianship Regulation for review (for example decisions about where you live or about services)
      `who is seeking review` IS A `Who is seeking review` @desc Who would apply. One of: "I am, as the person the decision is about", "my spouse", "the person who has the care of me", "someone the Tribunal considers adversely affected by the decision", "someone not listed in section 80A"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can this person seek review of the Public Guardian's decision` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the decision was made by the Public Guardian as my guardian under this Act`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (outside the grant in s 80A(1), which has no "only")
           IF (NOT `the decision is of a class prescribed by the regulations`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (outside the grant in s 80A(1); the regulation is not deposited)
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER `who is seeking review`
               WHEN `someone not listed in section 80A` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 80A(2) lists without "only")
               OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 101 -- keeping information about me confidential`

-- s 101 "A person shall not disclose any information obtained in connection with the administration or execution of this
-- Act unless the disclosure is made-- (a) with the consent of the person from whom the information was obtained, (b) in
-- connection with the administration or execution of this Act or the Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 2013, (c) for
-- the purposes of any legal proceedings arising out of this Act or the Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 2013 or of any
-- report of any such proceedings, (d) in accordance with a requirement imposed under the Ombudsman Act 1974, or (e) with
-- other lawful excuse. Maximum penalty--10 penalty units or imprisonment for 12 months, or both." "Lawful excuse" is
-- asked. Consent is that of "the person from whom the information was obtained", who may not be the person it is about
-- (finding 7).
DECLARE `The disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `with the consent of the person who gave the information`
    `in administering or executing this Act or the Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 2013`
    `for legal proceedings arising out of those Acts, or a report of them`
    `under a requirement under the Ombudsman Act 1974`
    `with some other lawful excuse`
    `for none of these reasons`

@export May information about me obtained under the Guardianship Act be disclosed this way (s 101)?
GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A `The disclosure` @desc How or why the information would be disclosed. One of: "with the consent of the person who gave the information", "in administering or executing this Act or the Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 2013", "for legal proceedings arising out of those Acts, or a report of them", "under a requirement under the Ombudsman Act 1974", "with some other lawful excuse", "for none of these reasons"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May information about me be disclosed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the disclosure`
    WHEN `for none of these reasons` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 101 "shall not disclose ... unless"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 101: the most a person can be fined or imprisoned for disclosing it unlawfully. A penalty unit's value is set by the
-- Crimes (Sentencing Procedure) Act 1999, s 17 (not deposited): the answer is in units.
@export What is the most someone who unlawfully discloses information about me can be fined (in penalty units) under s 101?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`The most penalty units for unlawful disclosure` MEANS 10

@export What is the longest someone who unlawfully discloses information about me can be imprisoned (in months) under s 101?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`The longest imprisonment in months for unlawful disclosure` MEANS 12
